   "source": [
    "## SLIDE 4-5: ¿Qué es una Subconsulta y Cómo se Evalúa?\n",
    "\n",
    "**Subconsulta:** Consulta SQL dentro de otra consulta.\n",
    "\n",
    "**Tipos:**\n",
    "1. **Escalares**: Devuelven UN valor\n",
    "2. **De columna**: Devuelven lista de valores (1 columna)\n",
    "3. **De tabla**: Devuelven filas y columnas (en FROM)\n",
    "4. **Correlacionadas**: Usan datos de consulta externa"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "print(\"=\"*70)\n",
    "print(\"SLIDE 5-6: Tipos de Subconsultas y Flujo de Evaluación\")\n",
    "print(\"=\"*70 + \"\\n\")\n",
    "\n",
    "print(\"Tipo 1: SUBCONSULTA ESCALAR (devuelve 1 valor)\")\n",
    "print(\"-\"*70)\n",
    "\n",
    "# Subconsulta escalar en SELECT\n",
    "query_escalar = '''\n",
    "SELECT \n",
    "    nombre,\n",
    "    precio_venta,\n",
    "    (SELECT AVG(precio_venta) FROM productos) as promedio_general\n",
    "FROM productos\n",
    "LIMIT 3\n",
    "'''\n",
    "\n",
    "print(\"\\nConsulta - Subconsulta escalar en SELECT:\")\n",
    "print(query_escalar)\n",
    "print(\"\\nResultado (primeros 3):\")\n",
    "df_escalar = pd.read_sql(query_escalar, conn)\n",
    "print(df_escalar.to_string())\n",
    "print(\"\\n✓ La subconsulta devuelve 1 valor (promedio_general)\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "print(\"\\nTipo 2: SUBCONSULTA DE COLUMNA (devuelve lista)\")\n",
    "print(\"-\"*70)\n",
    "\n",
    "# Subconsulta de columna en WHERE\n",
    "query_columna = '''\n",
    "SELECT \n",
    "    nombre,\n",
    "    precio_venta\n",
    "FROM productos\n",
    "WHERE categoria_id IN (\n",
    "    SELECT id FROM categorias WHERE nombre IN ('Lácteos', 'Panadería')\n",
    ")\n",
    "ORDER BY nombre\n",
    "'''\n",
    "\n",
    "print(\"\\nConsulta - Subconsulta de columna en WHERE:\")\n",
    "print(query_columna)\n",
    "print(\"\\nResultado:\")\n",
    "df_columna = pd.read_sql(query_columna, conn)\n",
    "print(df_columna.to_string())\n",
    "print(\"\\n✓ La subconsulta devuelve lista de IDs (1, 3)\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "print(\"\\nTipo 3: SUBCONSULTA DE TABLA (en FROM - tabla derivada)\")\n",
    "print(\"-\"*70)\n",
    "\n",
    "# Subconsulta de tabla en FROM\n",
    "query_tabla = '''\n",
    "SELECT \n",
    "    categoria_id,\n",
    "    promedio_precio\n",
    "FROM (\n",
    "    SELECT \n",
    "        categoria_id,\n",
    "        ROUND(AVG(precio_venta), 2) as promedio_precio,\n",
    "        COUNT(*) as cantidad\n",
    "    FROM productos\n",
    "    GROUP BY categoria_id\n") AS tabla_derivada\n",
    "WHERE cantidad >= 3\n",
    "'''\n",
    "\n",
    "print(\"\\nConsulta - Subconsulta de tabla en FROM:\")\n",
    "print(query_tabla)\n",
    "print(\"\\nResultado:\")\n",
    "df_tabla = pd.read_sql(query_tabla, conn)\n",
    "print(df_tabla.to_string())\n",
    "print(\"\\n✓ La subconsulta devuelve tabla (alias OBLIGATORIO)\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## SLIDE 7-8: Buenas Prácticas y Flujo de Evaluación"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "print(\"\\n\" + \"=\"*70)\n",
    "print(\"SLIDE 7-8: Flujo de Evaluación de Subconsultas\")\n",
    "print(\"=\"*70 + \"\\n\")\n",
    "\n",
    "print(\"Paso 1: IDENTIFICACIÓN\")\n",
    "print(\"  SQL identifica subconsultas dentro de paréntesis\\n\")\n",
    "\n",
    "print(\"Paso 2: EJECUCIÓN\")\n",
    "print(\"  Ejecuta subconsulta primero (generalmente)\\n\")\n",
    "\n",
    "print(\"Paso 3: TRANSFERENCIA\")\n",
    "print(\"  Resultado se transfiere a consulta principal\\n\")\n",
    "\n",
    "print(\"Paso 4: COMPARACIÓN/INTEGRACIÓN\")\n",
    "print(\"  Consulta principal usa resultado\\n\")\n",
    "\n",
    "print(\"-\"*70)\n",
    "print(\"\\n✓ BUENA PRÁCTICA 1: Validar subconsultas individualmente\")\n",
    "print(\"-\"*70)\n",
    "\n",
    "# Validar subconsulta por separado\n",
    "print(\"\\nPrimero, verificar subconsulta sola:\")\n",
    "query_sub = '''\n",
    "SELECT \n",
    "    categoria_id,\n",
    "    ROUND(AVG(precio_venta), 2) as promedio\n",
    "FROM productos\n",
    "GROUP BY categoria_id\n",
    "'''\n",
    "\n",
    "df_sub = pd.read_sql(query_sub, conn)\n",
    "print(df_sub.to_string())\n",
    "print(\"\\nLuego integrar en consulta mayor (con ALIAS)\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "print(\"\\n✓ BUENA PRÁCTICA 2: Usar alias en tablas derivadas (OBLIGATORIO)\")\n",
    "print(\"-\"*70)\n",
    "\n",
    "# CON ALIAS\n",
    "query_con_alias = '''\n",
    "SELECT categoria, promedio\n",
    "FROM (\n",
    "    SELECT \n",
    "        categoria_id as categoria,\n",
    "        ROUND(AVG(precio_venta), 2) as promedio\n",
    "    FROM productos\n",
    "    GROUP BY categoria_id\n") AS stats  -- ALIAS OBLIGATORIO\n",
    "WHERE promedio > 3.0\n",
    "'''\n",
    "\n",
    "print(\"\\nCon alias (CORRECTO):\")\n",
    "print(query_con_alias)\n",
    "print(\"\\nResultado:\")\n",
    "df_alias = pd.read_sql(query_con_alias, conn)\n",
    "print(df_alias.to_string())"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## SLIDE 9-11: Reglas Técnicas y Errores Comunes"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "print(\"\\n\" + \"=\"*70)\n",
    "print(\"SLIDE 10-11: Reglas Técnicas y Errores\")\n",
    "print(\"=\"*70 + \"\\n\")\n",
    "\n",
    "print(\"REGLAS TÉCNICAS:\")\n",
    "print(\"-\"*70)\n",
    "print(\"1. Alias obligatorio: Tablas derivadas (FROM) necesitan alias\")\n",
    "print(\"2. Compatibilidad de tipos: Subconsulta y comparación deben coincidir\")\n",
    "print(\"3. IN vs =: Usar IN si subconsulta devuelve múltiples valores\")\n",
    "print(\"4. Nivel de anidación: Evitar excesivas subconsultas (performance)\\n\")\n",
    "\n",
    "print(\"ERRORES COMUNES:\")\n",
    "print(\"-\"*70)\n",
    "\n",
    "print(\"\\n✗ ERROR 1: Olvidar alias en tabla derivada\")\n",
    "print(\"Incorrecto:\")\n",
    "print(\"\"\"SELECT * FROM (\n",
    "    SELECT categoria_id, AVG(precio_venta)\n",
    "    FROM productos\n",
    "    GROUP BY categoria_id\n",
    ")  -- ERROR: Falta alias\n",
    "\"\"\")\n",
    "print(\"Correcto:\")\n",
    "print(\"\"\"SELECT * FROM (\n",
    "    SELECT categoria_id, AVG(precio_venta)\n",
    "    FROM productos\n",
    "    GROUP BY categoria_id\n",
    ") AS tabla_derivada  -- ✓ Con alias\n",
    "\"\"\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "print(\"\\n✗ ERROR 2: Usar = con subconsulta que devuelve múltiples valores\")\n",
    "print(\"Incorrecto:\")\n",
    "print(\"\"\"SELECT nombre FROM productos\n",
    "WHERE categoria_id = (\n",
    "    SELECT id FROM categorias WHERE nombre IN ('Lácteos', 'Carnes')\n",
    ")  -- ERROR: devuelve 2 valores, no 1\n",
    "\"\"\")\n",
    "print(\"Correcto:\")\n",
    "print(\"\"\"SELECT nombre FROM productos\n",
    "WHERE categoria_id IN (\n",
    "    SELECT id FROM categorias WHERE nombre IN ('Lácteos', 'Carnes')\n",
    ")  -- ✓ IN para múltiples valores\n",
    "\"\"\")\n",
    "\n",
    "print(\"\\n✗ ERROR 3: No verificar tipos de datos\")\n",
    "print(\"Incorrecto:\")\n",
    "print(\"\"\"SELECT nombre FROM productos\n",
    "WHERE precio_venta = (SELECT id FROM categorias)  -- Tipos diferentes\n",
    "\"\"\")\n",
    "print(\"Correcto:\")\n",
    "print(\"\"\"SELECT nombre FROM productos\n",
    "WHERE categoria_id = (SELECT id FROM categorias LIMIT 1)  -- Tipos coinciden\n",
    "\"\"\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
